  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": null,
      "what": "The study analyzes the relationship between regional development and economic resilience across 897 European NUTS 3 regions during the COVID-19 pandemic. It constructs a multidimensional 'left behindness' index to move beyond traditional GDP metrics, finding that left-behind regions resisted the initial pandemic shock better, whereas more developed regions recovered more quickly.",
      "why": "It demonstrates that regional economic resilience is not a single attribute; instead, vulnerability and recovery capacity are decoupled, meaning less-developed regions possess inherent resistance mechanisms while developed regions possess superior recovery dynamics."
    }
